{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Any man, if his wife goes astray.</b> What is written above the passage? ״וְאִישׁ אֶת קֳדָשָׁיו לוֹ יִהְיוּ״ — if you withhold the priestly gifts, by your life you will need to come to him, to bring him the sotah." "<b>Any man.</b> To teach you that she betrays two — the Man of war above, and her husband below." "<b>For his wife goes astray.</b> Our Sages taught: adulterers do not commit adultery until a spirit of folly enters them, as it is written ״כִּי תִשְׂטֶה״ and it is written about him ״נֹאֵף אִשָּׁה חֲסַר לֵב״ (Proverbs 6); and the plain sense of Scripture: <b>for she goes astray</b> — she deviates from the ways of modesty and becomes suspect in his eyes, like ״שְׂטֵה מֵעָלָיו וַעֲבֹר״ (ibid. 4), ״אַל יֵשְׂטְ אֶל דְּרָכֶיהָ לִבֶּךָ״ (ibid. 7)." "<b>And commit a trespass against him.</b> And what is the trespass? <b>And a man lies with her.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:32.053050204Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}